    {
      "block_id": 2,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "In addition, you need to allocate memory to store the playfield, set pointers to tell the system \nwhere to find the data in memory, and (optionally) write a Copper routine to handle redisplay of \nthe playfield.\n",
      "bbox": [
